# ''[[che]]'', the fourth letter of the Spanish alphabet, after ''[[C]]'' and before ''[[D]]''

====Usage notes====
Since 1994, this letter has been treated as if it were ''[[C]]'' followed by ''[[h]]'' for collation purposes only.  Otherwise, it is considered as a distinct letter.

